CONFIRMA — PROJECT RULES FOR CURSOR

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
FOUNDATION — NEVER REBUILD, NEVER BYPASS
These are the load-bearing walls of the project.
Read before every task. Do NOT change any of these without
an explicit written request from the owner.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. CONFIRMATION PIPELINE — lib/confirmation/**
   - State machine: pending → confirmed | rejected | archived.
   - Reverse transitions are forbidden (confirmed → pending is illegal).
   - confirm-order.ts is the ONLY entry point for confirmation.
   - purchase-delivery.ts orchestrates ad delivery (Meta, TikTok, Google).
   - NEVER add shipping calls to the confirm route.
   - NEVER call ad delivery from anywhere except the confirm route.
   - Each ad platform is wrapped in its own try/catch.
     A failure in one MUST NOT block the others.

2. AUTH & SESSION — lib/auth/**
   - getAuthenticatedUser() is the ONLY way to identify a user.
   - NEVER trust user id from request body, query string, or URL.
   - NEVER expose SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to the client.
   - Google OAuth uses lib/auth/google-oauth.ts.

3. RLS & DATA ISOLATION
   - Every query MUST be scoped by owner_id = auth.uid()
     OR by a trusted store row the user owns.
   - Service-role writes MUST include owner_id from a trusted source
     (session, verified webhook, or store lookup). NEVER from client input.
   - Adding a new table: enable RLS, add SELECT policy, scope writes.

4. ORDER PIPELINE
   - Flow: Store webhook → HMAC verify → normalize → persist.
   - NEVER skip HMAC verification for WooCommerce or YouCan webhooks.
   - NEVER persist an order without owner_id from the store row.
   - Normalizers live in lib/integrations/<provider>/orders/normalize.ts.

5. AD DELIVERY
   - Meta, TikTok, Google deliver ONLY after a confirmed status change.
   - Every send is logged to ad_events_log (payload + status + http_status).
   - NEVER send an ad event for a pending or rejected order.
   - NEVER retry automatically. The merchant retries manually.

6. INTEGRATION BOUNDARIES
   - Each integration has its own client, secrets, and base URL.
   - NEVER cross-import between integrations.
   - Custom carrier webhook header: X-Confirma-Signature.
     This name is FROZEN. Renaming breaks downstream carriers.
   - Secrets are encrypted with SHIPPING_SESSION_SECRET or
     YOUCAN_SESSION_SECRET. NEVER log decrypted secrets.

7. DATABASE SCHEMA
   - Migrations are IMMUTABLE once applied. Never edit an applied file.
   - New changes = new migration file.
   - NEVER drop a column, table, or RLS policy without explicit request.
   - NEVER rename an existing table or column.
   - database/migrations/ and supabase/migrations/ MUST stay in sync.

8. EVENT MODEL (foundation for COD Network and future services)
   - The system is built around EVENTS, not around providers.
   - Events: ORDER_CONFIRMED, ORDER_DELIVERED, ORDER_CANCELLED.
   - Event source can be: MANUAL, COD_NETWORK, SERVICE_B, SERVICE_C.
   - The Event Router decides the destination, NOT the source.
   - Manual confirmation and automated confirmation MUST use the SAME router.
   - NEVER write "if provider === cod-network" in business logic.
   - Every provider is an Adapter. Each adapter declares its Capabilities.

9. PRODUCT IDENTITY (foundation for mapping)
   - Internal product has: id, name, sku, variant.
   - External IDs are stored per integration (YouCan ID, COD Network ID,
     Meta Content ID, TikTok Content ID, Google Item ID).
   - Auto-map first. Ask the user ONLY when auto-map fails.
   - NEVER request product mapping during onboarding.
   - Mapping UI appears ONLY when an integration reports it needs it.

10. ADVERTISING DESTINATIONS
    - Meta = active. TikTok = reserved. Google = reserved.
    - Adding a new destination = new Adapter file + registry entry.
    - NEVER add a destination that bypasses the Event Router.

11. PAYMENTS (when added)
    - Webhook signature verification is MANDATORY.
    - Idempotency keys are MANDATORY.
    - NEVER store raw card data.

12. RENAMING (Confirma → Onafirm)
    - User-visible text: replace freely.
    - X-Confirma-Signature: FROZEN. Do NOT rename.
    - Storage keys (confirma-*): FROZEN unless a migration plan exists.
    - Salt strings (confirma-*-token): FROZEN. Renaming breaks decryption.
    - Env variable names: change ONLY if no running service depends on them.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

These rules apply to EVERY task unless the user explicitly overrides them.
Read this file fully before touching anything.

SECRETS & ENVIRONMENT — NEVER TOUCH
- .env, .env.local, .env.*, any variant
- *.key, *.pem, *.p12, *.jks, *.keystore
- Any file containing: secret, token, apikey, private
- .vercel/, .supabase/

DATABASE & MIGRATIONS — NEVER TOUCH
- database/**, supabase/**
- Any *.sql file
- Any migration file

DEPENDENCIES & BUILD — NEVER TOUCH
- node_modules/, .next/, dist/, build/, coverage/, .turbo/
- package-lock.json, yarn.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml

CONFIG — NEVER TOUCH WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL
- tsconfig.json, next.config.*, tailwind.config.*, postcss.config.*
- eslint.config.*, .eslintrc*, .prettierrc*, vitest.config.*, playwright.config.*

BUSINESS LOGIC — NEVER TOUCH WITHOUT EXPLICIT APPROVAL
- lib/auth/**, lib/confirmation/**, lib/billing/**
- lib/dashboard/**, lib/integrations/**, lib/orders/**, lib/connections/**
- lib/webhooks/**, app/api/**

UNTRACKED INTEGRATIONS — LEAVE ALONE
- lib/integrations/shipping/sendit/**
- lib/integrations/shipping/coliix/**
- app/api/integrations/shipping/**
- Any file under scripts/
- Any *REPORT*.md
- Any *.md at repo root

GIT OPERATIONS — STRICT RULES
- NEVER use --force or --force-with-lease
- NEVER rebase, amend, reset, cherry-pick, merge, or stash (unless explicitly asked)
- NEVER run git add -A, git add ., or git add -u
- ALWAYS use explicit file paths in git add
- NEVER switch branches without explicit permission
- NEVER push any branch except the one currently checked out
- NEVER add a Co-authored-by trailer or any trailer not explicitly requested
- ALWAYS run `git diff --cached --name-only` before every commit and verify only expected files are staged
- If a commit or push fails — STOP, report, wait. Do NOT improvise.

UI RULES
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion (use motion-safe: or media query)
- Use RTL-safe logical properties (start/end), NEVER left/right
- Match existing rounded corners, shadows, spacing, and typography scale
- Keep the indigo/teal palette
- All new user-facing strings MUST be added to BOTH messages/en/*.json AND messages/ar/*.json

AFTER EVERY CODE CHANGE
- Run: npx tsc --noEmit  — must pass with zero errors
- Run: npm run lint       — must pass (7 Ameex warnings are OK)
- Run: npm test           — must remain 347/347
- If any test fails — REVERT the change, report, wait

COMMUNICATION
- If a task is unclear — STOP and ask. Do NOT improvise.
- If a file is not in the allowed list — do NOT stage it. Report and wait.
- Smallest possible diff. No refactoring. No reformatting. No renames.
- No new dependencies without explicit approval.
- When reporting back, list: files changed, before/after, tsc/lint/test results, and any file you intentionally did NOT touch.
